ba1543-c378-4718-a5b5-800fba646138","position":{"commit_sha":"7ba2786b6cdd3f1fc09342e082a09619c0bac67c","position":"1787345115378266001-f3ba1543-c378-4718-a5b5-800fba646138"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"129cd85320cfbbcfa105be44eab051493746b8a6b6fd41c3c50f2147cbc6918d","event_uuid":"477dd41a-c7e5-4caa-bd63-1b663a58a6dd","position":{"commit_sha":"b49f0862d51fc4d6bc5fe52f74708dd5a8823391","position":"1787345121009002001-477dd41a-c7e5-4caa-bd63-1b663a58a6dd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787290309928978001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"92f6031e-dc2a-46d7-8e57-c538a1a8c592","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141"},{"link_uuid":"13920c00-8b4f-4995-b1d8-bbc8b878e529","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a2b0-736d-9432-4ef5"},{"link_uuid":"57cb7f9e-97e4-4a39-861c-e50ed4872ae4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0975-0140-7ad5-4d83"},{"link_uuid":"4decacbe-cc76-4c1e-9856-0da06b41f414","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e95f-33d7-bd03-48bd"},{"link_uuid":"7792b578-302d-47ce-888d-4dfb679eb45e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"488f-60e8-b033-4275"}],"description":"# Config-driven status mapping (map-or-drift, round-trip via rebar-status labels)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nStatus mapping is hardcoded: outbound reads built-in `local_to_jira_status` at CREATE/UPDATE;\ninbound inverts built-in `jira_to_local_status`, preferring a `rebar-status:<local>` label\nhardcoded to `blocked`/`cancelled`. A project needing a remap/collapse has no echo-safe path. Make\nit config-driven on the S1 core: **map-or-drift** (never coerce); remap/collapse round-trips via\n`rebar-status:`.\n\n## Dependency (prerequisite ticket)\n\nOn the S1 mapping core **[rebar:bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141]** (merged): `mapping_config` provides\n`load_mapping_config(root=None)` + `resolve_for_project(config, key, *, builtin) -> MappingLayer`\n(merges `builtin ← default ← projects.<KEY>`; `.status_map` local→Jira, `SKIP`=drop, ABSENT=drift).\n`local_to_jira_status` is the `builtin`, so no `[mapping]` ⇒ effective map = today's default.\n\n## Approach — one FORWARD seam; inbound stays reverse-map-free\n\nOnly **outbound (forward)** becomes per-project; inbound needs no reverse map/project key (the\n`rebar-status:` label makes every non-built-in status self-describing).\n\n1. **`config.py` — forward resolution.** Add\n   `effective_status_map(project_key, root=None) -> dict[str,str]` = `load_mapping_config(root)` +\n   `resolve_for_project(builtin=local_to_jira_status)`. The literal stays the parity-tested\n   fallback; `mapping_config` imported LAZILY (config.py stays stdlib-only).\n\n2. **Outbound consumers read the resolved map via the `OutboundMapper` Protocol.**\n   `outbound_differ._effective_status_map_for(ticket, mapping, repo_root)` resolves the ticket's\n   project (`projects_store.resolve_project`) and calls\n   `config.effective_status_map(project_key, root=repo_root)` — the `[mapping]` overlay is read\n   from the STORE ROOT (not the CWD, mirroring fetcher/preflight), threaded via a new\n   `OutboundDiffConfig.repo_root` populated in `run_differs`. The effective `status_map` (optional;\n   `None`→built-in) flows into both Protocol methods — `map_local_to_remote` (CREATE) and\n   `map_fields_to_remote` (UPDATE, via `compute_update_fields`); `_backend.py` + the two wrappers\n   gain the param. Shared map-or-drift lives in `outbound_mapper.resolve_outbound_status`, reached\n   by the UPDATE mapper (Cloud+DC) and both CREATE builders. `acli.transition_issue` is NOT\n   threaded (gets the already-mapped name).\n\n3. **Drift = leave Jira as-is, never a per-mutation failure.** Decided ONLY in the mapper: with\n   no entry for a local status it **omits the `status` field** (Jira unchanged) + a drift alert\n   (deduped per-status per-process so it doesn't re-flood stderr each pass), replacing today's\n   `.get(status,\"To Do\")` coerce. `preflight_status_mapping` runs AFTER the mapper\n   (`reconcile.py:485`): a drift carries no `status`, but a config REMAP emits a config-only Jira\n   NAME absent from the BUILT-IN keys∪values it tolerates → spurious warning. Widen it (and the\n   fetcher, step 5) to built-in ∪ a **NEW S2** `mapping_config.declared_status_names` (from\n   `reconcile.py:485` `repo_root`).\n\n4. **Generalised `rebar-status:` round-trip (built-in-reverse stamp rule).** Outbound\n   (`outbound_labels`): `target = forward.get(local)` (GUARDED `.get`, never a subscript). A\n   DRIFTED local (no target) → **no label**. Else stamp `rebar-status:<local>` **iff\n   `config.jira_to_local_status.get(target) != local`**. On the built-in map this selects\n   {blocked, cancelled} (`deleted` is lossy but excluded upstream via `excluded_statuses`) —\n   default stamping preserved. Under ANY config remap/collapse, every status whose Jira target\n   isn't the built-in canonical name for `<local>` is labelled → inbound recovers it. Inbound:\n   parse the `rebar-status:<local>` suffix, validating `<local>` against a vocabulary DERIVED from\n   `_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS` values ∪ `deleted` (cannot drift from a parallel literal) via one shared\n   helper; the plain `_JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS.get()` fallback stays correct since every non-built-in\n   status is labelled. (Malformed `[mapping]` fails closed via S1's `MappingConfigError`.)\n\n5. **Fetcher known-set widened.** `fetcher._known_jira_statuses` today reads only built-in\n   `jira_to_local_status` keys → a config-only status trips a spurious \"no reconciler mapping\"\n   warning. Widen to built-in ∪ `mapping_config.declared_status_names` (from `repo_root`).\n\n## Scope (files)\n\n- `config.py` — `effective_status_map` (forward, lazy `mapping_config`).\n- `outbound_differ.py` — `_effective_status_map_for(ticket, mapping, repo_root)`; `OutboundDiffConfig.repo_root`; thread `status_map` into CREATE/UPDATE + label diff.\n- `run_differs.py` — populate `OutboundDiffConfig.repo_root` from the pass `repo_root`.- `outbound_field_diff.py` — `compute_update_fields` forwards `status_map`.\n- `_backend.py` — `OutboundMapper` Protocol: OPTIONAL `status_map` (default None) on both map methods.\n- `adapters/jira/backend.py`, `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` — wrappers forward `status_map`; DC `_map_local_to_dc_fields` uses it (DC CREATE) w/ drift-omit.\n- `adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py` — shared `resolve_outbound_status` (map-or-drift, deduped alert); `map_fields_to_remote` (UPDATE).\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` — `_map_local_to_jira_fields` (Cloud CREATE), drift-omit.\n- `outbound_labels.py` — built-in-reverse stamp rule keyed on `config.jira_to_local_status` (guarded).\n- `inbound_fields.py` — generalised `rebar-status:<local>` recovery via a DERIVED vocab (shared helper).\n- `inbound_translate.py` / `apply_inbound_events.py` / `inbound_differ.py` — shared helper (retire `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL`); `_LOCAL_STATUS_VALUES` re-uses the derived vocab.\n- `applier.py` — re-export shared helper in `__all__`.\n- `mapping_config.py` — **add NEW** `declared_status_names(config)`: every Jira status NAME declared across config (`status_map` values ∪ `statuses`).\n- `fetcher.py` — widen `_known_jira_statuses` to built-in ∪ config-declared names.\n- `reconcile_helpers.py` — widen `preflight_status_mapping` set (optional `repo_root`).\n- `reconcile.py` — thread `repo_root` into the `preflight_status_mapping` call.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_status_mapping.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\n\nTier **in-process unit** — pure over the resolved map; tests hit REAL entry points; alerts are\nnon-fatal stderr via `capsys`.\n\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Effective forward map = `local_to_jira_status` ← `default` ← `projects.<KEY>` via S1\n  `resolve_for_project`; a non-default overlay changes the outbound target through the real mapper\n  — `test_status_config_effect`.\n- [x] An unmapped status **drifts**: the mutation omits `status` (Jira unchanged) + a non-fatal\n  warning, never skipped nor a failure — `test_unmapped_status_drifts`; the drift alert is deduped\n  per-status per-process — `test_drift_warning_deduped_within_pass`.\n- [x] A config remap AND a collapsed pair (OTHER than blocked/cancelled) round-trip losslessly via\n  `rebar-status:<local>` labels, recovered inbound without a reverse map —\n  `test_status_remap_roundtrip`/`test_status_collapse_roundtrip`.\n- [x] The `outbound_differ` seam resolves the per-project map and reads `[mapping]` from the\n  `repo_root`, not the CWD — `test_effective_status_map_for_resolves_project`,\n  `test_effective_status_map_for_honors_repo_root`.\n- [x] A config-only/remapped Jira status is tolerated by BOTH the fetcher known-set AND the\n  post-mapper `preflight_status_mapping` — `test_fetcher_known_includes_config`,\n  `test_preflight_tolerates_config_remap`.\n- [x] The duplicated `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` literal is retired for a shared helper\n  (re-exported in `applier.__all__`) whose recovery vocab is DERIVED (not a divergent literal),\n  covering every local status the stamp rule can emit — `test_status_label_helper_single_source`,\n  `test_recovery_vocab_covers_every_local_status`.\n- [x] `value_maps`↔`config` parity tests in `state/test_config.py` stay green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py","reason":"add effective_status_map forward resolution over the S1 mapping core (lazy import)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"resolve project key once; thread effective status_map into the CREATE/UPDATE Protocol calls and the status-annotation label diff"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_field_diff.py","reason":"compute_update_fields accepts and forwards status_map to map_fields_to_remote"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_backend.py","reason":"OutboundMapper Protocol: optional status_map on map_local_to_remote and map_fields_to_remote"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py","reason":"Cloud backend wrappers forward status_map to the shared mapper / outbound_fields"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","reason":"DC backend wrappers forward status_map; _map_local_to_dc_fields uses it for DC CREATE with built-in fallback and drift-omit"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py","reason":"shared map_fields_to_remote uses status_map (UPDATE, Cloud+DC); drift-omit on unmapped; built-in fallback"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py","reason":"_map_local_to_jira_fields uses status_map for Cloud CREATE; drift-omit; built-in fallback"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_labels.py","reason":"generalised rebar-status stamp rule keyed on built-in config.jira_to_local_status over the effective forward map"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py","reason":"generalised rebar-status:<local> label recovery via a shared parse helper; plain built-in reverse lookup unchanged"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py","reason":"use the shared rebar-status parse helper; retire the duplicated _REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL literal"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py","reason":"use the shared rebar-status parse helper; retire the duplicated literal"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py","reason":"use the shared rebar-status parse helper in place of the imported literal"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"re-export the shared parse helper in __all__ in place of the retired literal"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"widen _known_jira_statuses to built-in plus config-declared Jira status names so a config-only status is not flagged unmapped"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_status_mapping.py","reason":"new behavioral oracle: config-effect, drift, remap/collapse round-trip, fetcher known-set, label-helper single-source"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_config.py","reason":"add declared_status_names(config) so the fetcher can union config-declared Jira status names"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_characterization.py","reason":"update the Cloud UPDATE characterization from coerce-to-To-Do to map-or-drift (unmapped status omitted)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py","reason":"update the DC CREATE/UPDATE characterization to map-or-drift (unmapped status omitted)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py","reason":"recording OutboundMapper test double accepts the new optional status_map kwarg"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_canonical_outbound_equivalence.py","reason":"injected OutboundMapper test double accepts the new optional status_map kwarg"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py","reason":"widen preflight_status_mapping tolerated set to include config-declared Jira names (repo_root param) so a per-project remap is not false-flagged"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"thread repo_root into the preflight_status_mapping call"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py","reason":"populate OutboundDiffConfig.repo_root from the reconcile pass repo_root so the per-project [mapping] overlay is read from the store root, not the CWD"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141"],["parent","3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"],["relates_to","0975-0140-7ad5-4d83"],["relates_to","488f-60e8-b033-4275"],["relates_to","a2b0-736d-9432-4ef5"],["relates_to","e95f-33d7-bd03-48bd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_status_uuid":"f3ba1543-c378-4718-a5b5-800fba646138","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"438a-e1d9-29d3-4081","ticket_type":"story","title":"Config-driven status mapping (map-or-drift, collapse round-trip via rebar-status labels)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["16507100-9ef9-45bc-a9cb-34323e0ccd50","13920c00-8b4f-4995-b1d8-bbc8b878e529","57cb7f9e-97e4-4a39-861c-e50ed4872ae4","e44cf6e5-0f34-47f3-b61c-08398c85372a","04a996e0-0dff-476c-bb7b-860caf54aef7","4f079272-f51d-4c89-8129-f867483e33ac","7510324b-edf1-4802-b648-4abaf934d1b4","4decacbe-cc76-4c1e-9856-0da06b41f414","be6c622a-9063-486c-a3b2-48916f385e04","7792b578-302d-47ce-888d-4dfb679eb45e","7c134f5f-f08c-4ba0-a97b-96c6fc0bb4d7","f3ba1543-c378-4718-a5b5-800fba646138","477dd41a-c7e5-4caa-bd63-1b663a58a6dd"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787354427365312001,"uuid":"06441d18-9177-4712-a8c5-f2cb02ee3315"}